sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: stage 2 and stage 4 of the command development pipeline (docs/reference/pipeline/2-development-environment.mmd, 4-pr-and-ci.mmd). A task VM holds no GitHub credential, so the workspace cannot fetch. The author needs the branch of the pull request and main when either moved on origin (a merge of main into the branch, a correction pushed by the owner), to merge or rebase before the push. Decided by the orchestrator, for Nick's review.
  %% Task copy (2026-11-14): the same kind brings the Project's default branch into a task copy through the copy's Node mirror and one incremental bundle; no credential enters the copy and the branch is never merged or rebased. The run selects the copy path by the intent key `copy`; the task VM steps read only the keys they read before, so a run that an older Gateway admitted keeps its task VM path. Task VMs get no new work. docs/reference/tasks.md#bring-main-into-a-copy.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: task:sync
  %% kind: tasks.sync
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane GH icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Task VM, Node<br/>reached over ssh
  participant GH as GitHub<br/>origin
  CLI->>GW: task:sync 42<br/>refresh the refs
  %%> Command:
  %%> - the MCP tool `task-sync`, or `POST /api/v1/tasks/42/sync` with an `Idempotency-Key` and no body
  Note over GW: Admit the sync<br/>group 42 · capture the intent
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to the Gateway
  %%> - group 42 is open and external, with its own task VM workspace and a pushed branch `task-42`, or with its own task copy
  %%> - a task VM runs; a parked VM is woken by the admission, which answers `tasks.vm_resuming`
  %%> - a task copy's container runs, else `tasks.instance_not_running`, and no copy turn of the group is unended, else `tasks.copy_turn_unended`
  %%> - no other task runs on group 42, so no check or publish; the Gateway holds one lock per group
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - captures the repository, the default branch, the branch `task-42`, the workspace path and the SSH target of the VM
  %%> - for a task copy, adds `copy`: its Node's SSH target, its container, its start commit and its Node mirror
  %%> - names the vault key of the read credential
  %%> Decided by the orchestrator, for Nick's review:
  %%> - no Swamp step calls the Gateway: the Gateway mints the read token (`contents: read`, valid one hour) as it starts the run and writes it to that vault key, as it does for the Pi token of a turn; the run gets only the key name
  %%> - each run mints its own credential; a later run never reuses it
  GW->>SW: Start one run, full intent<br/>operation-task-sync
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - the whole intent above and the vault key name of the read credential, never the credential
  %%> - no step of the run calls the Gateway
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>Operation recorded
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the Operation with `operation:show`
  alt a task copy
    SW->>N: Bring in the base<br/>workspace phase base
    %%> On the Node:
    %%> - first removes what an earlier, cancelled sync of the copy left in the copy's Node scratch and bundle folder, which the copy's Instance names
    %%> - writes the read credential to a file in that scratch, mode 0600, readable by root only, and removes it in an `always` block; it never enters the container
    %%> - fetches `+refs/heads/<default>` from the Project's repository into the copy's own mirror, `/var/lib/orbit/instance-repositories/<instance>.git`; a missing mirror is made from the default's mirror first
    %%> - bundles the default branch without the commits the copy already holds (`^origin/<default>`, `^task-42`, where the mirror holds them); when the copy holds the head already, no bundle is made
    %%> In the container, as `agent`:
    %%> - `git fetch` of the bundle into `refs/remotes/origin/<default>` only
    %%> - reads the default head, the branch commit, `git rev-list --count task-42..origin/<default>` and the copy's start
    %%> Result:
    %%> - HEAD, the working tree, the index and the local branches are not touched; nothing is merged or rebased
    %%> Source:
    %%> - the Project's repository, for every Project; a Project whose repository receives main only at a release sees the last released main
    SW->>N: Discard the base scratch<br/>workspace phase base-cleanup
    %%> When:
    %%> - always: after success, failure or a cancelled run
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - removes the copy's credential file and bundle on the Node and the bundle in the container
    %%> - a cancelled run may skip this step; the next sync of the copy removes the same scratch before its fetch
    %%> Test:
    %%> - a failed and a cancelled sync leave no credential file on the Node and no bundle in the copy
  else a task VM
    SW->>GH: Clone the refs<br/>git clone --bare · fetch
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - on Node 209, in a scratch directory of the run: a bare clone of the default branch and a fetch of `task-42`, with the token, read from its vault key, as an extra header of the commands and nowhere else
    SW->>SW: Bundle the refs<br/>git bundle create
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - one bundle of the default branch and `task-42`
    SW->>N: Prepare the VM directory<br/>mkdir -m 0700
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - a private directory of the run on the VM
    SW->>N: Copy the bundle<br/>official SSH copy
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - copies the bundle into that directory; no token and no script reaches the VM
    SW->>N: Fetch the refs<br/>git fetch · bundle
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - `git fetch` of the bundle into `refs/remotes/origin/<default branch>` and `refs/remotes/origin/task-42` of the workspace
    %%> Result:
    %%> - HEAD, the working tree and the local branches are not touched; the author merges or rebases itself, as the review of the stage asks
    SW->>N: Read the refs<br/>git rev-parse
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - reads the two commits the fetch stored
    SW->>SW: Clean up the scratch<br/>rm -rf
    %%> When:
    %%> - always, on success and failure: the scratch directory of the run on Node 209
    SW->>N: Clean up the VM directory<br/>rm -rf
    %%> When:
    %%> - always, after the scratch: the run's directory on the VM
  end
  Note over SW: Confirm the sync
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - native assert: for a task VM, the read and both clean ups succeeded; for a task copy, the base and its discard succeeded
  alt synced
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event · commits
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Record the result<br/>refs · behind_by
    %%> Result:
    %%> - a task VM: the commit of the default branch and the commit of `task-42`
    %%> - a task copy: `default_branch`, `default_commit`, `branch`, `branch_commit`, `behind_by` and `start`
  else a step failed
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code · failed step
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed; a branch that does not exist on origin fails the clone step
    Note over GW: Mark the Operation failed<br/>workspace unchanged
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - run it again: a new run mints a new credential, and a fetch that already happened makes the next bundle smaller
  end
  loop until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show<br/>Operation number
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the Operation status, and the commits and `behind_by` when the run succeeded
  end
